# Problem #10 — Product of Array Except Self

Given an array of integers, return an array where each element is the product of every value except the one at the current index.

## Approach

For each index:

```text
result[i] = left product × right product
```

Use two passes without an additional working array.

**Left-to-right pass:** store the product of all elements to the left of each index.

**Right-to-left pass:** maintain a running right product and multiply it into the stored left product.

**Time:** O(n)
**Space:** O(1) extra space, excluding the output array.

## Key Learning

* Break a complex calculation into reusable left and right accumulations.
* Use the output array to store intermediate results when extra arrays are restricted.
* A running product can replace repeated multiplication.

## SDET Relevance

This pattern is useful when processing API or test-data collections where each result depends on aggregated information from both sides of an element.
